        question: "What are the ownership and use tests for the Section 121 exclusion?",
        answer:
          "The ownership test requires owning the home for at least two years during the five years before the sale. The use test requires using the home as a principal residence for at least two years during that same period. Both tests must generally be satisfied to claim the full exclusion.",
